# Vue components

Complements @vue-components-style.mdc (CSS) and @project-structure.mdc (file locations).

## Script

New components use `<script setup lang="ts">`. Type props and emits. Use `withDefaults` for defaults. Derived values go in `computed`, not in the template.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { computed } from 'vue'

interface Props {
  name: string
  adopted?: boolean
}

const props = withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), {
  adopted: false,
})

const emit = defineEmits<{
  adopt: []
}>()

const cardClasses = computed(() => ({
  'animal-card--adopted': props.adopted,
}))
</script>
```

- Refs: explicit types (`ref<boolean>(false)`). Booleans: `is` / `has` / `should`.
- Template refs: `ref<HTMLInputElement | null>(null)`.
- Reusable logic: `src/composables/useX.ts`. Keep store/API access in pages and containers; small components take props and emit events.
- Async: `try/catch/finally`; reset loading in `finally`. Clean timers/listeners in `onUnmounted`.

## Accessibility

Interactive elements need a name (`aria-label` or visible text). Errors: `role="alert"`. Loading: `role="status"`. Inputs have a label.

## Icons

Use `AppIcon` (`@/shared/components/AppIcon.vue`) for every icon. `AppIcon` is decorative (`aria-hidden`); the control keeps the accessible name (`aria-label` or visible text). Do not import `~icons/` outside `src/shared/components/app-icon.registry.ts`. Add a Lucide name to `APP_ICON_NAMES` and the registry when a new icon is needed.

## daisyUI modals

Keep `modal-box` in the template. Teleport to `body`. Close via `<form method="dialog" class="modal-backdrop">`.

```vue
<Teleport to="body">
  <div v-if="show" class="modal modal-open">
    <div class="modal-box">
      <!-- content -->
    </div>
    <form method="dialog" class="modal-backdrop">
      <button type="submit">close</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</Teleport>
```

## CSS

Follow @vue-components-style.mdc: semantic classes, `@apply` in `<style scoped>`, `@reference "@/styles/main.css"`.

